<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">2 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 2 August, from 216 BCE to 1990.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">216 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,241 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hannibal annihilates a Roman army at Cannae</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthaginians</a> encircled and destroyed a much larger Roman army in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, killing perhaps 50,000 men. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cannae">Cannae</a> remains the classic model of a battle of encirclement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/punic-empire">Punic Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/49-bce">49 BCE</a> <span class="tih-ago">2,074 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pompey's legates Afranius and Petreius surrender to Caesar at Ilerda</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After early successes, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legatus">legates</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-petreius">Marcus Petreius</a> and Lucius Afranius, were forced to capitulate to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lleida">Ilerda</a> and disband their army. Caesar let them go free, and they travelled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> to join Pompey.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-petreius">Marcus Petreius</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">47 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,072 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Julius Caesar defeats Pharnaces II at the Battle of Zela</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zela">Zela</a>, now a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharnaces-ii-of-pontus">Pharnaces II</a>, who had tried to reconquer Pontus during the Roman civil war. The victory was reported as 'veni, vidi, vici'.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharnaces-ii-of-pontus">Pharnaces II of Pontus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">932 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,094 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Toledo surrenders to Abd al-Rahman III after a two-year siege</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a two-year siege, the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliph</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, who had promised them immunity. It was an important victory in his campaign to subjugate the Central March.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate-of-cordoba">Emirate of Córdoba</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Delegates sign the engrossed Declaration of Independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Most members of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-congress">Continental Congress</a> signed the parchment copy of the Declaration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philadelphia">Philadelphia</a>. By signing, they put their names to an act of treason in British eyes.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1870">1870 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">156 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Tower Subway opens beneath the Thames</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A cable-hauled railway carriage began carrying passengers through the Tower Subway in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>. Bored with a tunnelling shield, it was the world's first tube railway, though it closed within months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1923">1923 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">President Warren Harding dies in San Francisco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Warren Harding died suddenly during a western tour, and Vice President Calvin Coolidge was sworn in by his father by lamplight in Vermont. The Teapot Dome scandal soon tarnished Harding's memory.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1934">1934 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">92 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler becomes Führer on Hindenburg's death</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-von-hindenburg">Paul von Hindenburg</a> died, and a law passed the day before merged the presidency with the chancellorship. Hitler became head of state and the army swore an oath of loyalty to him personally.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1990">1990 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">36 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Iraq invades Kuwait</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a>'s forces overran Kuwait in a matter of hours. A US-led coalition expelled them in early 1991, though Saddam remained in power.</p></div></li></ol>
