<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 2 August <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-england"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-ii-of-england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William II of England</span><span class="tp">c. 1056–1100</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/raymond-vi-count-of-toulouse"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/raymond-vi-count-of-toulouse.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Raymond VI, Count of Toulouse</span><span class="tp">1156–1222</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-of-burgundy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis of Burgundy</span><span class="tp">1297–1316</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/christopher-ii-of-denmark"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/christopher-ii-of-denmark.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Christopher II of Denmark</span><span class="tp">1276–1332</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/kato-kiyomasa"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/kato-kiyomasa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Katō Kiyomasa</span><span class="tp">1562–1611</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/muhammad-ali-of-egypt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Muhammad Ali of Egypt</span><span class="tp">1769–1849</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/paul-von-hindenburg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/paul-von-hindenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Paul von Hindenburg</span><span class="tp">1847–1934</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
